# Normalise line endings on the way into git, and check every text file out
# with LF regardless of platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone gets CRLF from core.autocrlf and
# `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` fails on every line of every file:
#
#   ServiceStatusTests.cs(21,60): error ENDOFLINE: Fix end of line marker.
#
# .editorconfig already says end_of_line = lf, so the formatter is right and
# the checkout is wrong. CI runs on Linux and never sees it, which makes this
# the worst shape of disagreement: the gate passes in CI and fails locally, so
# the developer who tries to reproduce a green build cannot.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must not be touched by the rules above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.snk binary
